{
  "message": "Good news: the local Azurite run for revision 2 passed with no failures. That means the generated storage code can upload, read and delete objects against a local stand-in, but it doesn't prove real Entra permissions, versioning, region availability or a real Terraform plan, so there's nothing on the diagram to fix right now. The biggest open item is where the data lives, because that decides whether australiaeast is the right region: should these synthetic documents stay in Australia, or can they be stored in another country?",
